1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,763
A colleague just left the company.

2
00:00:02,763 --> 00:00:06,091
Behind them: a Tomcat server nobody has looked at.

3
00:00:06,091 --> 00:00:07,156
It is yours now.

4
00:00:07,706 --> 00:00:09,139
The cart does not load.

5
00:00:09,139 --> 00:00:11,381
The server answers on every network.

6
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:13,935
And the stop word is the factory default.

7
00:00:14,485 --> 00:00:19,776
This is the Tomcat mastery lesson. You use what you learned in eight lessons, in one job.

8
00:00:20,326 --> 00:00:22,459
Find it, fix it, harden it, prove it.

9
00:00:24,009 --> 00:00:25,502
One job, five moves.

10
00:00:26,052 --> 00:00:30,426
One: read. Start the server, and let the log tell you why the cart fails.

11
00:00:30,976 --> 00:00:34,624
Two: recover. Redeploy the last good release, and read the health.

12
00:00:35,174 --> 00:00:39,782
Three: harden. Listen on the local machine only, and change the stop word.

13
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:43,980
Four: prove. A health script, and a lab check that judges you.

14
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:49,415
Five: write it down. A short report: what you found, fixed, proved, and cleaned.

15
00:00:49,965 --> 00:00:52,440
Read, recover, harden, prove, report.

16
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:59,375
Go to the lab folder. Type: cd /opt/lab112.

17
00:01:00,925 --> 00:01:02,824
Look around. Type: ls.

18
00:01:03,374 --> 00:01:07,406
Releases and settings.

19
00:01:07,956 --> 00:01:11,519
One good release: cart 1.0. And one settings file.

20
00:01:12,069 --> 00:01:14,863
Read the settings.

21
00:01:16,413 --> 00:01:19,955
Only the currency. Remember: there is no shop name yet.

22
00:01:20,505 --> 00:01:27,289
Start the inherited server, and keep the last line.

23
00:01:27,839 --> 00:01:36,948
Ask the cart for its status line.

24
00:01:42,298 --> 00:01:46,202
404, not found. The server is up, but the cart is not.

25
00:01:46,752 --> 00:01:53,707
Why? Ask the Catalina log.

26
00:01:54,257 --> 00:01:57,942
A document must start and end within the same entity.

27
00:01:57,942 --> 00:02:00,654
In plain words: a tag was never closed.

28
00:02:00,654 --> 00:02:03,366
The release has a broken web.xml.

29
00:02:03,916 --> 00:02:10,188
Redeploy the last good release, as cart.war.

30
00:02:10,738 --> 00:02:14,834
Tomcat notices the new file, and replaces the app within seconds.

31
00:02:15,384 --> 00:02:24,067
Ask the health page.

32
00:02:24,617 --> 00:02:24,939
Down.

33
00:02:24,939 --> 00:02:27,326
The shop.name setting is missing.

34
00:02:27,326 --> 00:02:28,552
The cart loads now,

35
00:02:28,552 --> 00:02:30,810
but its health says it is not well.

36
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:32,681
A page is not a health check.

37
00:02:33,231 --> 00:02:39,524
Add the missing setting.

38
00:02:40,074 --> 00:02:41,525
Ask the health page again.

39
00:02:44,475 --> 00:02:49,253
Up, CloudCart. Recovered. Now the second half of the job: the server itself.

40
00:02:49,803 --> 00:02:54,241
Who can reach this port? Ask the sockets.

41
00:02:54,791 --> 00:02:58,407
Look at the address: 0.0.0.0.

42
00:02:58,407 --> 00:03:00,863
Every network can reach this server.

43
00:03:00,863 --> 00:03:03,047
Only the local machine needs to.

44
00:03:03,597 --> 00:03:06,413
Stop the server first.

45
00:03:07,763 --> 00:03:08,519
Why stopped?

46
00:03:08,519 --> 00:03:12,426
The stop word is read from the same file we are about to edit.

47
00:03:12,426 --> 00:03:13,624
Edit while it runs,

48
00:03:13,624 --> 00:03:16,019
and the stop script no longer matches.

49
00:03:16,569 --> 00:03:21,091
Open the config in vim.

50
00:03:21,641 --> 00:03:23,396
Search for the port: /

51
00:03:23,396 --> 00:03:24,955
8088,

52
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:25,345
Enter.

53
00:03:25,345 --> 00:03:25,800
Then A,

54
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:31,583
to add at the end of the line: address="127.0.0.1".

55
00:03:32,133 --> 00:03:33,250
Now the stop word.

56
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:34,492
Search for shutdown,

57
00:03:34,492 --> 00:03:37,472
and change the word SHUTDOWN to one of your own.

58
00:03:37,472 --> 00:03:38,341
Save and quit.

59
00:03:39,891 --> 00:03:41,619
Start the server again.

60
00:03:43,969 --> 00:03:47,211
Look at the sockets again.

61
00:03:47,761 --> 00:03:50,666
127.0.0.1.

62
00:03:50,666 --> 00:03:52,220
The local machine only.

63
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:54,652
The server is closed to the network.

64
00:03:55,202 --> 00:03:56,418
And the app still works.

65
00:03:59,668 --> 00:04:02,100
Up, CloudCart. Hardened, and healthy.

66
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:04,975
Now a health script. Write it in vim.

67
00:04:06,125 --> 00:04:08,741
The same five lines as before: the shell,

68
00:04:08,741 --> 00:04:09,506
the address,

69
00:04:09,506 --> 00:04:10,527
the status code,

70
00:04:10,527 --> 00:04:11,484
a printed line,

71
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:12,632
and the exit code.

72
00:04:18,182 --> 00:04:20,998
Success only on 200. Save and quit.

73
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:28,612
Make it executable.

74
00:04:29,162 --> 00:04:31,423
Run it.

75
00:04:32,473 --> 00:04:34,820
Health, 200. Exit code 0.

76
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:37,695
Last file: the report. Four lines that start with found, fixed, proof, and clean up.

77
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:40,930
Found: a broken web.xml,

78
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:42,386
and a missing setting.

79
00:04:42,386 --> 00:04:43,974
Fixed: the good release,

80
00:04:43,974 --> 00:04:44,900
the shop name,

81
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,091
the local address,

82
00:04:46,091 --> 00:04:47,415
and a new stop word.

83
00:04:52,465 --> 00:04:58,011
Proof: health says 200, and lab check passes. Clean up: lab down. Save and quit.

84
00:05:08,361 --> 00:05:09,620
Now the judge.

85
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:16,578
Five lines, five passes. Five out of five.

86
00:05:17,128 --> 00:05:19,944
Clean up. Stop the server.

87
00:05:21,294 --> 00:05:22,062
Stopped.

88
00:05:22,612 --> 00:05:27,156
Prove the port is free. Count the lines.

89
00:05:27,706 --> 00:05:32,058
Zero. Nothing is listening. Read, recover, harden, prove, report.

90
00:05:33,608 --> 00:05:36,168
Your task. Take over the inherited server.

91
00:05:36,718 --> 00:05:40,153
One: start it, and read the log. Find why the cart fails.

92
00:05:40,703 --> 00:05:45,161
Two: redeploy the good release, and fix the missing setting, until health says up.

93
00:05:45,711 --> 00:05:49,338
Three: close the server to the network, and change the stop word.

94
00:05:49,888 --> 00:05:53,109
Four: write health.sh, and a four line report.

95
00:05:53,659 --> 00:05:56,262
Then run lab check. All five must pass.

96
00:05:58,312 --> 00:06:02,515
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

97
00:06:03,065 --> 00:06:04,713
The lab lives on GitHub,

98
00:06:04,713 --> 00:06:05,880
at it-waves,

99
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,459
/devops-ai,

100
00:06:07,459 --> 00:06:08,970
in the folder academy,

101
00:06:08,970 --> 00:06:09,657
/lab.

102
00:06:10,207 --> 00:06:15,199
Two files: lab112.sh, and shortcuts112.sh.

103
00:06:15,749 --> 00:06:16,653
Install it,

104
00:06:16,653 --> 00:06:19,532
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

105
00:06:19,532 --> 00:06:21,423
-m 755,

106
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:23,315
lab112.sh,

107
00:06:23,315 --> 00:06:24,548
into /usr,

108
00:06:24,548 --> 00:06:25,535
/local,

109
00:06:25,535 --> 00:06:26,522
/sbin.

110
00:06:27,072 --> 00:06:31,979
Load the short name with: source shortcuts112.sh. You get: lab.

111
00:06:32,529 --> 00:06:33,625
You need a JDK,

112
00:06:33,625 --> 00:06:33,948
curl,

113
00:06:33,948 --> 00:06:35,045
and the ss tool,

114
00:06:35,045 --> 00:06:36,916
about one gigabyte of memory,

115
00:06:36,916 --> 00:06:41,755
and ports 8088 and 8098 free.

116
00:06:41,755 --> 00:06:43,174
No systemd is needed.

117
00:06:43,724 --> 00:06:45,491
Lab check judges your work.

118
00:06:45,491 --> 00:06:48,435
Lab down stops Tomcat and removes everything.

119
00:06:48,435 --> 00:06:50,529
Only run it on your own machine.

120
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:54,648
Pass or fail. You need all six.

121
00:06:55,198 --> 00:06:57,012
Five pass lines in lab check.

122
00:06:57,562 --> 00:07:02,084
The log showed the broken web.xml, and the cart answers 200.

123
00:07:02,634 --> 00:07:08,650
Port 8088 listens on 127.0.0.1 only.

124
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,462
The stop word is no longer the default.

125
00:07:12,012 --> 00:07:14,465
Shop.name is set, and health says up.

126
00:07:15,015 --> 00:07:19,388
Health.sh exits with zero, and the report has its four lines.

127
00:07:19,938 --> 00:07:21,240
To pass, all six.

128
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:25,061
Your turn, on your own machine.

129
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,341
One: lab up, read the task list, start Tomcat.

130
00:07:28,891 --> 00:07:31,281
Two: find why the cart fails, in the log.

131
00:07:31,831 --> 00:07:34,796
Three: redeploy the good release, and fix the setting.

132
00:07:35,346 --> 00:07:39,207
Four: bind the port to the local address, and change the stop word.

133
00:07:39,757 --> 00:07:42,765
Five: the health script, the report, and lab check.

134
00:07:43,315 --> 00:07:45,897
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

135
00:07:46,447 --> 00:07:48,281
Pause the video, and begin now.

136
00:08:03,831 --> 00:08:04,706
Quick check.

137
00:08:05,256 --> 00:08:07,645
Which log showed why the cart failed to start?

138
00:08:08,195 --> 00:08:11,118
Why stop Tomcat before changing the stop word?

139
00:08:11,668 --> 00:08:16,105
What does 0.0.0.0 mean in the socket list?

140
00:08:16,655 --> 00:08:18,596
Why write a report after the fix?

141
00:08:19,146 --> 00:08:22,478
Objective covered: MC12 mastery evidence.

142
00:08:22,478 --> 00:08:23,896
An inherited Tomcat,

143
00:08:23,896 --> 00:08:24,534
repaired,

144
00:08:24,534 --> 00:08:25,172
hardened,

145
00:08:25,172 --> 00:08:25,952
and proved.

146
00:08:26,502 --> 00:08:28,571
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

147
00:08:39,121 --> 00:08:43,174
Next: CloudCart, version zero, built and deployed to Tomcat.

148
00:08:43,724 --> 00:08:47,052
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
